[Applause]  [Music]  give me one minute and i'll show you how  cloud pubs up can help you keep your  services reliably communicating with  each other  cloud pub sub is an asynchronous  messaging service which means it helps  your tools send receive  and filter events or data streams it  gives you durable message storage  scalable in-order message delivery  consistently high availability and  performance at any scale  and pub sub runs in any google cloud  region in the world so you can easily  use it in jakarta  frankfurt or montreal and of course  everywhere else  you also don't have to provision pub sub  it scales global data delivery  automagically from zero to millions of  messages per second  with pub sub data producers don't need  to change anything when the consumers of  their data change  just publish once and let us manage  distribution this lets more of your  services be entirely stateless  you set up pub sub between services or  applications by defining topics  and then subscriptions which allows  services to receive the messages  published on those topics  this means one-to-many communication  gets much simpler  so you can spread batch image analysis  over multiple workers  or send logs from your security system  to archiving processing and analytics  services  or if you've got a steady stream of data  you can use pub sub to stream that data  into bigquery or dataflow for  intelligent processing  pub sub is really handy for notification  when something bad happens so you can  page the right teams if a system or  service goes  down so next time you need a way to  connect multiple services  applications or data sources take a  minute to try out cloud pub sub  learn more at cloud.google.com pub sub  you

